## Deploy-gate precondition

D-11 step 3 forbids touching the production dataset until the Phase 2 English filter is
live on production and the production build has been regenerated. Confirmed before the dry
run below was started:

`.planning/phases/03-translation-pipeline/artifacts/deploy-gate.md` carries a **Post-deploy**
section. Its gate verdict reads:

> D-11 step 2 is **closed**. The repaired lockfile installed cleanly on Vercel (the
> deploy built and reached Ready, which is the T-03-11 evidence pass for the three
> too-new package bumps), production runs the Phase 2 English filter, the Studio split
> and the 18-field schema, and the production dataset holds zero Farsi documents.

Supporting facts recorded in that section: the push moved `origin/main` `5ea9ddb..43b5dfe`,
Vercel deployment `dpl_A16hZgLQZJozQsmvXq8NkY8C8qmD` reached READY with
`gitSource.sha` byte-identical to the pushed HEAD and the apex domain aliased to it, the
live filter check exited 0 against `blog_posts`, and the post-deploy raw-perspective count
read `language fa : 0`.

The precondition holds. The dry run below was the first command this plan ran against the
production dataset.

