which is the same post that failed twice on the dev run for an unrelated reason.

### Known risk carried in from plan 03-09

03-09 diagnosed a per-call defect: the model can return an empty string for a slot whose
source is the bare English definite article `"The "` immediately before an inline link.
Persian has no definite article, so the response is defensible in isolation, but an empty
leaf stops being a translatable slot and the structural fingerprint gate then refuses the
write. It blocked roughly one dev post in six. The fix belongs to the code and was not made
in this plan.

The dry run does **not** print string contents, so this pattern is not visible in the
capture above and no additional production query was run to look for it, the dry run being
the only read this dispatch permits against `blog_posts`. What is known without any further
query is that both dev posts 03-09 diagnosed the defect on are also production candidates,
with the same slugs and the same block keys:

| Slug | Block | Diagnosed on the dev run |
|---|---|---|
| `why-explainable-ai-matters-more-than-you-think` | k51 | `["The ", "EU AI Act", ", which enters its enforcement phase in August 2026, ..."]` |
| `what-neuronomixer-stands-for-ai-data-and-the-future-of-systems` | k114 | `["The ", "European Commission defines Industry 5.0", " through three pillars: ..."]` |

Those two are the only production candidates known to carry the pattern. Any of the other
24 may carry it undetected. The defect is per call rather than per post: both dev posts
blocked and then passed on a later attempt with nothing changed.

