## Authorisation

Given 2026-08-25, in session, at the plan 03-10 Task 1 blocking checkpoint. The per-post
breakdown above was put in front of Saeid first, and three slugs were recommended from it.
He selected:

> "industry-50-explained (Recommended)"

Resolved slug:

```
industry-50-explained-why-the-future-is-human-centred-not-just-automated
```

Scope authorised: **one post**. `--all` with `--execute` was not authorised and is forbidden
by the plan; the 26-post backlog sweep belongs to Phase 5.

Why this post was the recommendation, restated so the choice is checkable rather than taken
on trust: 33 table cells, 135 spans and 3 image alts across 173 strings and 19,592
characters. It exercises D-13 table-cell translation and image alt text together in one
document, at roughly two thirds the token volume of the largest candidate, and it is
evergreen and European-framed rather than a time-stamped news roundup. It is also not one
of the two candidates known to carry the `"The "` empty-string pattern.

Nothing had been written to the production dataset at the time this authorisation was
recorded. The dry run above was the only command that had touched `blog_posts`.

